  "summary_en": "Bahrain's 2017 Cloud First Policy directs government entities to evaluate cloud services in all ICT procurement to cut costs, improve security and productivity. It covers cloud definitions (NIST), migration criteria, security, data classification, data sovereignty, and roles of iGA, ICTGC and SCICT. It has no AI or robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "All government agencies must evaluate cloud-based services in ICT procurements.",
   "Adopts NIST definition of cloud computing and service/deployment models.",
   "Covers security principles, data classification, backup and data sovereignty.",
   "iGA acts as interface with cloud providers and monitors SLAs.",
   "ICTGC oversees implementation and audits entities for compliance."
  ],
